# Run & deploy workbooks

The build loop: author, verify, run locally, then ship — each step one command with a runnable
confirmation, not a "did it work?" guess.

**When to use:** iterating on a workbook — checking it, running it locally, or deploying it.

## The loop
- **Author + check** — write `.work`, then `work check` (resolves every reference + audits capabilities). A
  clean check is your go-ahead. `work structure` lists the units; `work why | near | wit` answer dependency
  questions.
- **Weave** — `work weave <dir> <out>` produces the one shippable artifact.
- **Run locally** — `work dev <dir>` watches + re-weaves on change (with nexus hot-swap) at
  `http://localhost:4000`. `work deploy local` is the prod simulation (a vfkit micro-VM on macOS).
- **Ship** — `work deploy` mounts the workbook into a running nexus; `work deploy verify | status | down`
  health-probe, inspect, tear down. The cloud target is `app.workbooks.sh` (Fly).

## The discipline
- **Verify each step** — exit codes + artifacts confirm success; don't vibe it.
- **Local before cloud** — `work dev` / `work deploy local` catch what cloud would, cheaply.
- **Non-interactive flags** — never let a deploy hang.
